    {
      "id": 188134,
      "name": "hstein3",
      "username": "hstein3",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/hstein3/{size}/2159_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-01-17T13:58:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Interesting – since Vengeance-format villains are incapped <strong><em>instead</em></strong> of destroyed, they probably don’t trigger the “on destruction” effects of the bounties? Could also depend on the bounty, as they don’t all work the same.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=12\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Specifically, the bounty was “Kill on Sight;” when the target leaves play, the bountu is destroyed and CR draws 3 cards. I’d assumed that incapping the main villain would trigger the effect. When it didn’t, I got curious.</p>",
